{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared golden vectors for the CSV export. Loaded by BOTH the Android (JVM) and",
    "iOS (Swift) suites.",
    "escapeField = rfc4180Quote(neutralizeFormula(raw)): the OWASP formula guard runs",
    "first, then RFC 4180 quoting wraps the guarded value if structurally required.",
    "buildCsv emits CRLF line endings and terminates the LAST record with CRLF too.",
    "Only free-text cells (headers, drinkName, note) are escaped; generated cells",
    "(logicalDate, time, category, numbers) are not, exactly as on Android.",
    "The UTF-8 BOM is added when writing the file, not by buildCsv.",
    "utcOffsetSeconds renders the HH:mm column: the entry carries the frame its clock time was read in, and the same instant is a different clock time in a different frame. The cases used to name a zoneId instead, which stood in for entries that recorded no offset; schema 4 gave every row one, so the offset is stated per entry. Each value is mechanically the offset Europe/Berlin had at that instant, so every expected string is unchanged.",
    "From v0.87.0 column 1 is the CALENDAR day of the reading and a ninth column at the end carries the logical day. The two agree for every entry outside the small hours; where they differ, the row's date and time now describe the same moment and the attribution has a column of its own."
  ],
  "escapeField": [
    {
      "description": "plain value untouched",
      "input": "Pils",
      "expected": "Pils"
    },
    {
      "description": "empty stays empty",
      "input": "",
      "expected": ""
    },
    {
      "description": "comma forces quoting",
      "input": "Wine, red",
      "expected": "\"Wine, red\""
    },
    {
      "description": "double quote is doubled and wrapped",
      "input": "He said \"hi\"",
      "expected": "\"He said \"\"hi\"\"\""
    },
    {
      "description": "line feed forces quoting",
      "input": "line1\nline2",
      "expected": "\"line1\nline2\""
    },
    {
      "description": "bare carriage return forces quoting",
      "input": "line1\rline2",
      "expected": "\"line1\rline2\""
    },
    {
      "description": "equals sign is a formula trigger",
      "input": "=1+1",
      "expected": "'=1+1"
    },
    {
      "description": "plus sign is a formula trigger",
      "input": "+1",
      "expected": "'+1"
    },
    {
      "description": "minus sign is a formula trigger",
      "input": "-5 today",
      "expected": "'-5 today"
    },
    {
      "description": "at sign is a formula trigger",
      "input": "@SUM(A1)",
      "expected": "'@SUM(A1)"
    },
    {
      "description": "leading tab is a formula trigger",
      "input": "\t=1+1",
      "expected": "'\t=1+1"
    },
    {
      "description": "leading CR is a trigger and then forces quoting",
      "input": "\r=1+1",
      "expected": "\"'\r=1+1\""
    },
    {
      "description": "a leading CRLF is a trigger too, one grapheme or two",
      "input": "\r\n=1+1",
      "expected": "\"'\r\n=1+1\""
    },
    {
      "description": "a quote is doubled even when a combining mark follows it",
      "input": "say \"́ now",
      "expected": "\"say \"\"́ now\""
    },
    {
      "description": "hyperlink attack is neutralised",
      "input": "=HYPERLINK(\"http://evil\",\"click\")",
      "expected": "\"'=HYPERLINK(\"\"http://evil\"\",\"\"click\"\")\""
    },
    {
      "description": "trigger only matters at the start",
      "input": "a=1+1",
      "expected": "a=1+1"
    },
    {
      "description": "guard then quote compose",
      "input": "=a,b",
      "expected": "\"'=a,b\""
    }
  ],
